# --- Usenet acquisition service (SABnzbd 5.1.3) runtime closure -------------
# The acquisition service is bundled INSIDE this image, so its Python runtime
# dependencies are DebridPulse runtime dependencies and must participate in the
# one shipped lock: a second, unhashed install transaction would both escape
# --require-hashes and be free to replace packages this lock already selected.
# These are the service's own Linux runtime pins (SABnzbd-5.1.3/requirements.txt).
# Deliberately NOT carried over from that file:
#   * its test tooling (pytest, selenium, black, tavern, flask, lxml, ...) --
#     test tooling is not a runtime dependency and has no place in the image;
#   * its win32/darwin entries, which cannot apply here;
#   * its defensive re-pins of packages this lock already resolves (cffi,
#     pycparser, certifi, idna, urllib3, charset_normalizer, six,
#     python-dateutil, cryptography and the requests/apprise sub-dependencies),
#     which would otherwise downgrade packages DebridPulse already ships.
